|---|---|
| National Bureau of Statistics (NBS, 国家统计局) | Chinese government data; use per the notice on its own site |
| World Bank Open Data | CC BY 4.0 |
| IMF DataMapper / WEO | IMF copyright; attribution required |
| FRED (Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis) | Each series belongs to its original publisher; FRED only redistributes |
| BIS | Redistributes national official statistics under BIS copyright |

**Check these terms before redistributing anything harvested by this tool.**
Running the tool and using the output for your own analysis is one thing;
republishing a merged dataset is another.

The `examples/` folder in the distributable zip contains data snapshots taken
during development. They are covered by the terms above, not by MIT.

## Why this file exists separately

GitHub detects a project's licence by parsing `LICENSE`. Appending non-licence
text to that file makes the detection fail and the repository shows up as
"NOASSERTION" instead of "MIT". Keeping the data note here keeps both facts
true at once: the code is unambiguously MIT, and the data caveat is still
stated in the repository.

## Third-party components

The install-free zip built by `tools/make-dist-zip.py` bundles:

- **CPython 3.12.7** (Python Software Foundation License) — the embeddable
  Windows distribution from python.org
- **PyYAML 6.0.3** (MIT)
- **pip 26.2.1** (MIT)

Everything else in `python/econ_core/` is this project's own code, and the
HTTP layer uses only the Python standard library.
